-- title:
--   Maximal ideal of W[[u,v]]/(uv-π) is (u,v)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring that is local, and let $\pi \in W$ be an element generating the maximal ideal, i.e. $\mathfrak m_W = (\pi)$. Write `UVCrossingModel W π` for the quotient of the two-variable formal power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (Mathlib's `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed as a constant power series; thus `UVCrossingModel W π` is the crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi)$. Assume, as a typeclass hypothesis, that this quotient is itself a local ring (this is not derived here). Then the maximal ideal of `UVCrossingModel W π` is the ideal generated by the two elements `U π` and `V π` of the quotient — the project's two branch coordinates, which satisfy $U\pi \cdot V\pi =$ `const π π`, the class of the constant $\pi$. So $\mathfrak m = (u,v)$: two generators suffice, the constant $\pi$ being redundant.
--
--   This is the width-one case $uv = \pi$ of the Mazur–Rapoport local models for modular curves at a supersingular point of $\Gamma_0(p)$-level structure; for $uv = \pi^e$ with $e \ge 2$ the maximal ideal $(u,v,\pi)$ genuinely requires three generators. Within the project it feeds the regularity statement [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.isRegularLocalRing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.isRegularLocalRing) for this local model, a comparison with adic completions, and the Cerednik–Drinfeld statement on deformations of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair.lean

